
# Earth System Digital Twin – Rainfall Forecasting

## Project Overview
Developed a deep learning-based rainfall prediction model to downscale coarse-resolution climate data into higher-resolution precipitation estimates for Punjab, Pakistan.

The project explores the use of Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) neural networks and geospatial data processing to support localized climate analysis.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Deep Learning (LSTM)
- ERA5 Climate Data
- Geospatial Data Processing
- GRIB and GeoTIFF

## Key Contributions
- Developed an LSTM-based model to estimate precipitation at a spatial resolution of 25 km.
- Processed ERA5 climate variables and incorporated spatial and temporal information into the modeling pipeline.
- Built a data-processing pipeline involving GRIB-to-GeoTIFF conversion, resampling, normalization, and sequence generation.
- Evaluated model performance using Mean Squared Error (MSE), Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), and Mean Absolute Error (MAE).

